---
import Layout from "../../layouts/Layout.astro";
---

<Layout
  title="Miranda · Selected Work · UX & Product Consultant"
  description="Selected projects: complex software, operational workflows, data-driven products and digital systems. Design decisions, real problems, clear reasoning."
  page="work-en"
  bg='data-max="110" data-link="150" data-accent="0.08" data-speed="0.12"'
>

  <!-- HERO -->
  <section class="page-hero">
    <div class="shell">
      <div class="eyebrow reveal">Selected work</div>
      <h1 class="reveal d1">I don't just design screens. I design the system that makes them work.</h1>
      <p class="reveal d2">A selection of projects across different contexts: complex software, operational workflows, data-driven products and visual direction. In some cases the output is highly visible. In others, the best work is what the user no longer has to think about.</p>
      <div class="casi-anchors reveal d3">
        <a class="casi-anchor" href="#edilarte">UI &amp; Visual Direction</a>
        <span class="casi-anchor-sep" aria-hidden="true">·</span>
        <a class="casi-anchor" href="#health">Complex Product</a>
        <span class="casi-anchor-sep" aria-hidden="true">·</span>
        <a class="casi-anchor" href="#sordo">Workflow &amp; Data</a>
        <span class="casi-anchor-sep" aria-hidden="true">·</span>
        <a class="casi-anchor" href="#wec">Strategy</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- ─────────────────────────── CASE 01 · EDILARTE -->
  <section class="section tight caso-section" id="edilarte">
    <div class="shell">

      <div class="caso-eyebrow-row reveal">
        <span class="pill wine"><span class="dot"></span>UI &amp; Visual Direction</span>
        <span class="caso-num">01</span>
      </div>

      <div class="lead-2col reveal d1" style="margin-top:22px;align-items:start;gap:48px;">
        <div>
          <h2 class="h2-cinema" style="max-width:16ch;">From product catalogue to brand experience.</h2>
        </div>
        <div>
          <p style="font-size:17px;line-height:27px;margin-top:0;">Edilarte Piracci is a family business with fifty years of experience in home furnishing and materials. The existing site was essentially a product catalogue. The new project had to bring the quality of their showroom, their expertise and their curation of brands online.</p>
          <a class="caso-link" href="https://edilartepiracci.vercel.app" target="_blank" rel="noopener">
            <i data-lucide="external-link" class="ic" aria-hidden="true"></i> See the live site
          </a>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- Before / After -->
      <div class="ba-grid reveal d2" style="margin-top:48px;">
        <div class="ba-col ba-before">
          <div class="ba-label">BEFORE · Product catalogue</div>
          <img src="/assets/piracci-before-home-desktop.webp" alt="Old Edilarte Piracci site: Products menu open with thirteen flat categories, no visual hierarchy, images used as decoration" class="caso-img" loading="lazy" />
          <p class="ba-caption">Many categories, little hierarchy, images used mainly as catalogue and a digital experience that didn't reflect the company's actual positioning.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="ba-col ba-after">
          <div class="ba-label">AFTER · Editorial experience</div>
          <img src="/assets/piracci-after-home-desktop.webp" alt="New Edilarte Piracci site: editorial direction, ambient photography, typography and space as identity elements" class="caso-img" loading="lazy" />
          <p class="ba-caption">A more editorial direction, built on photography, typography, rhythm, space and hierarchy to bring the site closer to the showroom experience.</p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- Visual detail sequence -->
      <div class="img-strip reveal d3" style="margin-top:40px;">
        <img src="/assets/piracci-after-design-system.webp"
          alt="Edilarte Piracci design system: components, Futura and DM Sans typography, blue-ochre-black palette, hero sections, product and room cards"
          class="caso-img caso-img-wide" loading="lazy" />
        <img src="/assets/piracci-after-materiali.webp"
          alt="Creative direction with the photographer: moodboard of material combinations (marbles, ceramics, fittings) that communicate the company's consultancy approach"
          class="caso-img" loading="lazy" />
        <img src="/assets/piracci-after-anima.webp"
          alt="About Us section of the new site: family identity, ambient photo collage, text on tailored consultancy"
          class="caso-img" loading="lazy" />
        <img src="/assets/piracci-after-prodotto.webp"
          alt="Hydrotherapy product page: gallery with lightbox, selected brands highlighted"
          class="caso-img" loading="lazy" />
      </div>
      <p class="strip-note reveal d3">The site is still being completed: some photographic and product content is awaiting delivery from the client.</p>

      <!-- Strategic shift -->
      <div class="holo glow-wine reveal d2" style="margin-top:52px;padding:32px 36px;">
        <div class="eyebrow" style="margin-bottom:12px;">The core repositioning</div>
        <p style="font-size:19px;font-weight:700;color:#fff;line-height:1.4;margin:0 0 16px;font-family:var(--font-heading);">From a showroom for other brands' products to a story about consultancy.</p>
        <p style="font-size:15px;line-height:25px;color:var(--on-dark-2);margin:0;">The old site displayed other manufacturers' products and linked directly to their own websites. The problem wasn't aesthetic: it was positioning. Edilarte is not a retailer that shows catalogues: it's a family business that selects major brands, pairs them to each client's specific needs and accompanies them from concept through to post-purchase. None of this came through on the old site. The new one is built to make it unmistakable: the consultancy is the product, the brands are the tools.</p>
      </div>

      <!-- Design decisions -->
      <div class="decisions reveal d2" style="margin-top:40px;">
        <div class="decision-label">Design decisions</div>
        <div class="decisions-grid">
          <div class="decision-item">
            <div class="decision-n">01</div>
            <div>
              <h4 class="decision-title">Reduce the noise</h4>
              <p class="decision-body">From a catalogue of categories to a few high-intent entry points. Fewer choices, clearer positioning.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div class="decision-item">
            <div class="decision-n">02</div>
            <div>
              <h4 class="decision-title">Give images more space</h4>
              <p class="decision-body">Visual material becomes part of the hierarchy, not decoration. Photography and material combinations as identity elements.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div class="decision-item">
            <div class="decision-n">03</div>
            <div>
              <h4 class="decision-title">Build recognisability</h4>
              <p class="decision-body">Typography, composition and rhythm used as identity rather than relying on a neutral template that would look like any other retailer.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- ─────────────────────────── CASE 02 · HEALTHCARE SYSTEM -->
  <section class="section tight caso-section caso-alt" id="health">
    <div class="shell">

      <div class="caso-eyebrow-row reveal">
        <span class="pill wine"><span class="dot"></span>Complex Product Design</span>
        <span class="caso-num">02</span>
      </div>

      <div class="lead-2col reveal d1" style="margin-top:22px;align-items:start;gap:48px;">
        <div>
          <h2 class="h2-cinema" style="max-width:18ch;">One system to coordinate people, information and operations.</h2>
        </div>
        <div>
          <p style="font-size:17px;line-height:27px;margin-top:0;">A custom management system for a distributed network of healthcare sites. Multiple roles, multiple schedules, multiple data flows that had to converge in a single operational interface without requiring extensive training.</p>
          <p style="font-size:13px;color:var(--on-dark-3);margin-top:12px;font-style:italic;">Real project · selected details have been anonymised for confidentiality.</p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- Roles and real flows -->
      <div class="holo reveal d1" style="margin-top:40px;padding:32px 36px;">
        <div class="eyebrow" style="margin-bottom:24px;">Who uses the system · what they do · what it propagates</div>
        <div class="ruoli-grid">

          <div class="ruolo">
            <div class="ruolo-label">Site operator</div>
            <div class="ruoli-flows-col">
              <div class="ruolo-flow">
                <span class="flow-tag">needs to check a regulation</span>
                <span class="fa">→</span>
                <span class="flow-tag">opens the portal</span>
                <span class="fa">→</span>
                <span class="flow-tag">types the name</span>
                <span class="fa">→</span>
                <span class="flow-tag">finds the document</span>
                <span class="flow-tag flow-tag-note">no email search needed</span>
              </div>
              <div class="ruolo-flow" style="margin-top:12px;">
                <span class="flow-tag">needs to update hours</span>
                <span class="fa">→</span>
                <span class="flow-tag">opens the portal</span>
                <span class="fa">→</span>
                <span class="flow-tag">edits in their profile</span>
                <span class="fa">→</span>
                <span class="flow-tag flow-tag-propagate">propagates to institutional site · public authority · citizen web app</span>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>

          <div class="ruolo" style="margin-top:20px;">
            <div class="ruolo-label">Schedule coordinator</div>
            <div class="ruolo-flow">
              <span class="flow-tag">divides sites by zone</span>
              <span class="fa">→</span>
              <span class="flow-tag">clicks "Generate schedule"</span>
              <span class="fa">→</span>
              <span class="flow-tag">algorithm computes 2 years</span>
              <span class="fa">→</span>
              <span class="flow-tag">row-level exceptions</span>
              <span class="fa">→</span>
              <span class="flow-tag flow-tag-propagate">propagates to citizen web app</span>
            </div>
          </div>

          <div class="ruolo" style="margin-top:20px;">
            <div class="ruolo-label">Citizen · 2:00 AM</div>
            <div class="ruolo-flow">
              <span class="flow-tag">opens the public portal</span>
              <span class="fa">→</span>
              <span class="flow-tag">accepts geolocation</span>
              <span class="fa">→</span>
              <span class="flow-tag flow-tag-ok">sees the nearest open site</span>
            </div>
          </div>

        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- The complexity -->
      <div class="complessita reveal d2" style="margin-top:40px;">
        <div class="eyebrow" style="margin-bottom:16px;">The complexity</div>
        <p style="font-size:15px;line-height:25px;color:var(--on-dark-2);margin:0 0 20px;max-width:68ch;">A single action in the portal propagates data across three different surfaces in real time. The operator who updates their hours doesn't know they're simultaneously updating the institutional site, the communication to the competent public authority and the web app a citizen will use at 2 AM to find the nearest open site. They don't need to know. They just need to change the hours.</p>
        <div class="complessita-chain">
          <div class="cc-node">Operator portal</div>
          <div class="cc-arr">→</div>
          <div class="cc-node">Institutional site</div>
          <div class="cc-arr">+</div>
          <div class="cc-node">Public authority</div>
          <div class="cc-arr">+</div>
          <div class="cc-node cc-node-out">Citizen web app</div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- Key problems -->
      <div class="problemi-list reveal d2" style="margin-top:40px;">
        <div class="eyebrow" style="margin-bottom:16px;">Key problems</div>
        <div class="scope-grid">
          <div class="scope" style="border-color:rgba(232,154,154,0.2);background:rgba(232,154,154,0.04);">
            <h4 style="color:#e89a9a;font-size:15px;font-weight:700;margin-bottom:10px;">01 · Three surfaces, zero synchronisation</h4>
            <p style="font-size:14.5px;line-height:23px;color:var(--on-dark-2);margin:0;">Hours, schedules and regulations lived in separate systems. Every update required manual intervention in each one. Misalignment errors were frequent and visible to citizens.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="scope" style="border-color:rgba(232,154,154,0.2);background:rgba(232,154,154,0.04);">
            <h4 style="color:#e89a9a;font-size:15px;font-weight:700;margin-bottom:10px;">02 · Schedules built by hand</h4>
            <p style="font-size:14.5px;line-height:23px;color:var(--on-dark-2);margin:0;">The schedule coordinator built duty rosters manually for dozens of sites on a two-year basis. Every change required recalculating the connected schedules from scratch.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- Design decision -->
      <div class="holo glow-wine reveal d2" style="margin-top:32px;padding:32px 36px;">
        <div class="eyebrow" style="margin-bottom:12px;">Design decision</div>
        <p style="font-size:19px;font-weight:700;color:#fff;line-height:1.4;margin:0 0 16px;font-family:var(--font-heading);">We designed the flow before designing the screens.</p>
        <p style="font-size:15px;line-height:24px;color:var(--on-dark-2);margin:0;">The data model and propagation logic were defined before drawing any interface. The goal wasn't to build a management system; it was to make one action in one place update everything else without the operator having to think about it.</p>
      </div>

      <!-- Flow comparison: schedules -->
      <div class="flow-comparison reveal d3" style="margin-top:48px;">
        <div class="eyebrow" style="margin-bottom:24px;">Flow comparison · Schedule management</div>
        <div class="flow-compare-grid">
          <div class="flow-col flow-col-before">
            <div class="flow-col-label">Before</div>
            <div class="flow-steps-vert">
              <div class="fv-step fv-pain">Collect data from each site</div>
              <div class="fv-arr">↓</div>
              <div class="fv-step fv-pain">Manual schedule calculation in a spreadsheet</div>
              <div class="fv-arr">↓</div>
              <div class="fv-step fv-pain">Update the institutional site separately</div>
              <div class="fv-arr">↓</div>
              <div class="fv-step fv-pain">Separate communication to the public authority</div>
              <div class="fv-arr">↓</div>
              <div class="fv-step fv-pain">Any change: start over from scratch</div>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div class="flow-compare-divider" aria-hidden="true">→</div>
          <div class="flow-col flow-col-after">
            <div class="flow-col-label">Designed flow</div>
            <div class="flow-steps-vert">
              <div class="fv-step fv-ok">Divide sites by zone</div>
              <div class="fv-arr">↓</div>
              <div class="fv-step fv-ok">Click "Generate schedule" · algorithm computes 2 years</div>
              <div class="fv-arr">↓</div>
              <div class="fv-step fv-ok">Any change: edit on the row</div>
              <div class="fv-arr">↓</div>
              <div class="fv-step fv-ok">Automatic propagation across all surfaces</div>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- UI output -->
      <div class="img-strip-4 reveal d3" style="margin-top:48px;">
        <div class="eyebrow" style="margin-bottom:20px;">Project output</div>
        <div class="farmacie-grid">

          <div class="farmacie-item farmacie-wide">
            <img src="/assets/farmacie-flusso.webp"
              alt="Full user flow of the public web app: splash page, geolocation, map with open site, site list, site detail with navigation and call CTA"
              class="caso-img" loading="lazy" />
            <p class="img-caption">Complete user flow: from splash page to the nearest open site, with both paths (geolocation active / inactive) and the databases connected to each screen.</p>
          </div>

          <div class="farmacie-item">
            <img src="/assets/farmacie-app-screens.webp"
              alt="iPhone screens of the citizen web app: nearest site with map, menu, site list with open/closed status, monthly schedule with calendar"
              class="caso-img" loading="lazy" />
            <p class="img-caption">Citizen web app: nearest site geolocated, real-time status (open, on duty, currently closed, on leave), monthly schedule with navigable calendar.</p>
          </div>

          <div class="farmacie-item">
            <img src="/assets/farmacie-profili-utente.png"
              alt="Operator portal architecture in Figma: three separate profiles with flows and screens for each"
              class="caso-img" loading="lazy" />
            <p class="img-caption">The operator portal structured around three profiles with distinct access levels and capabilities.</p>
          </div>

          <div class="farmacie-item">
            <img src="/assets/farmacie-sito-istituzionale.webp"
              alt="Institutional site homepage: hero with CTA Find the nearest open site and web app mockup"
              class="caso-img" loading="lazy" />
            <p class="img-caption">The institutional site: one of the surfaces that automatically receives updates whenever the operator portal is changed.</p>
          </div>

        </div>
      </div>

    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- ─────────────────────────── CASE 03 · SORDO AUTO -->
  <section class="section tight caso-section" id="sordo">
    <div class="shell">

      <div class="caso-eyebrow-row reveal">
        <span class="pill wine"><span class="dot"></span>Workflow &amp; Data Design</span>
        <span class="caso-num">03</span>
      </div>

      <div class="lead-2col reveal d1" style="margin-top:22px;align-items:start;gap:48px;">
        <div>
          <h2 class="h2-cinema" style="max-width:20ch;">When the management system becomes the place where the work actually happens.</h2>
        </div>
        <div>
          <p style="font-size:17px;line-height:27px;margin-top:0;">CRM, quotes, sales, rental, availability, automations and activities all lived in the same Odoo ecosystem, but not necessarily in the same flow. The project wasn't to configure Odoo. It was to translate operational requirements into system behaviour.</p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- Sales flow -->
      <div class="reveal d1" style="margin-top:44px;">
        <div class="eyebrow" style="margin-bottom:16px;">Flow · Sales</div>
        <div class="flow" style="gap:6px;flex-wrap:wrap;">
          <span class="node">Lead</span><span class="arr">→</span>
          <span class="node">Opportunity</span><span class="arr">→</span>
          <span class="node">Quote</span><span class="arr">→</span>
          <span class="node">Contract</span><span class="arr">→</span>
          <span class="node">Signature</span><span class="arr">→</span>
          <span class="node">Activities</span><span class="arr">→</span>
          <span class="node" style="border-color:rgba(110,207,151,0.5);color:#6fcf97;">Reporting</span>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- Rental flow -->
      <div class="reveal d2" style="margin-top:28px;">
        <div class="eyebrow" style="margin-bottom:16px;">Flow · Rental</div>
        <div class="flow" style="gap:6px;flex-wrap:wrap;">
          <span class="node">Availability</span><span class="arr">→</span>
          <span class="node">Selection</span><span class="arr">→</span>
          <span class="node">Booking</span><span class="arr">→</span>
          <span class="node">Deposit</span><span class="arr">→</span>
          <span class="node">Client check</span><span class="arr">→</span>
          <span class="node">Confirmation</span><span class="arr">→</span>
          <span class="node" style="border-color:rgba(110,207,151,0.5);color:#6fcf97;">Balance</span>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- Three concrete cases -->
      <div class="reveal d2" style="margin-top:52px;">
        <div class="eyebrow" style="margin-bottom:24px;">Three concrete cases</div>
        <div class="steps">
          <div class="step">
            <div class="n">0<span class="bg">1</span></div>
            <div>
              <h3>CRM: turning an opportunity into a tracked flow</h3>
              <p>Every lead had to generate automatic activities assigned to the right sales rep, with visible deadlines and a status that could be updated without leaving the client view. The operational need: no leads lost to oversight or lack of visibility on current state.</p>
              <div class="io">
                <span class="lbl">Need</span><span class="pill">no lost leads</span>
                <span class="lbl">Data</span><span class="pill">lead + sales rep + deadline</span>
                <span class="lbl">Output</span><span class="pill">automatic assigned activity</span>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div class="step">
            <div class="n">0<span class="bg">2</span></div>
            <div>
              <h3>Quote: from conversation to document in one step</h3>
              <p>The quote had to reflect real-time availability, current pricing and margins, and be sendable directly from the management system with integrated digital signature. The previous problem was the distance between negotiation and the formal document.</p>
              <div class="io">
                <span class="lbl">Inputs</span><span class="pill">availability + pricing + margins</span>
                <span class="lbl">Logic</span><span class="pill">auto calculation + approval</span>
                <span class="lbl">Output</span><span class="pill">signable quote from CRM</span>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div class="step">
            <div class="n">0<span class="bg">3</span></div>
            <div>
              <h3>Rental: availability, payment and verification in one flow</h3>
              <p>Booking a vehicle required checking availability, collecting a deposit, verifying client documents and confirming, often at separate times and through different channels. The project unified these steps into a sequential flow with explicit checkpoints.</p>
              <div class="io">
                <span class="lbl">Availability</span><span class="pill">real-time vehicle calendar</span>
                <span class="lbl">Payment</span><span class="pill">deposit + balance tracked</span>
                <span class="lbl">Verification</span><span class="pill">client docs + checklist</span>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- Flow diagram -->
      <div class="reveal d3" style="margin-top:52px;">
        <div class="eyebrow" style="margin-bottom:20px;">Flow mapping</div>
        <div class="sordo-flusso-wrap" id="sordo-zoom-wrap">
          <img
            src="/assets/sordo-odoo-flusso.webp"
            alt="Flow diagram of the Odoo system for Sordo Auto: sales flow and rental flow with all steps, states, actors and automations mapped in the to-be ideal"
            class="caso-img sordo-flusso-img"
            id="sordo-flusso-img"
            loading="lazy"
          />
          <button class="zoom-btn" id="sordo-zoom-btn" aria-label="Expand image">
            <svg width="18" height="18" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2"><path d="M15 3h6v6M9 21H3v-6M21 3l-7 7M3 21l7-7"/></svg>
            <span>Expand</span>
          </button>
        </div>
        <p class="img-caption" style="margin-top:10px;">To-be ideal mapping: sales flow (CRM, quote, order, warehouse, delivery) and rental flow (booking, verification, plates, return) with actors, states and automations.</p>
      </div>

      <!-- Lightbox -->
      <div class="sordo-lightbox" id="sordo-lightbox" role="dialog" aria-modal="true" aria-label="Odoo flow - Sordo Auto">
        <button class="lb-close" id="sordo-lb-close" aria-label="Close">✕</button>
        <img src="/assets/sordo-odoo-flusso.webp" alt="" class="lb-img" />
      </div>

    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- ─────────────────────────── CASE 04 · WEBSITE EVOLUTION CHECK -->
  <section class="section tight caso-section caso-alt" id="wec">
    <div class="shell">

      <div class="caso-eyebrow-row reveal">
        <span class="pill wine"><span class="dot"></span>Strategy · UX Audit</span>
        <span class="caso-num">04</span>
      </div>

      <div class="lead-2col reveal d1" style="margin-top:22px;align-items:start;gap:48px;">
        <div>
          <h2 class="h2-cinema" style="max-width:16ch;">Sometimes the best decision is to redesign nothing.</h2>
        </div>
        <div>
          <p style="font-size:17px;line-height:27px;margin-top:0;">The site had been live for years, traffic was coming in, conversions weren't. The temptation was a full redesign. The audit showed the problem was structural, not visual. Recommending less than the client expected was the hardest and the most correct decision.</p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- Key problems -->
      <div class="problemi-list reveal d2" style="margin-top:40px;">
        <div class="eyebrow" style="margin-bottom:16px;">Key problems</div>
        <div class="scope-grid">
          <div class="scope" style="border-color:rgba(232,154,154,0.2);background:rgba(232,154,154,0.04);">
            <h4 style="color:#e89a9a;font-size:15px;font-weight:700;margin-bottom:10px;">01 · A site that talks but doesn't convert</h4>
            <p style="font-size:14.5px;line-height:23px;color:var(--on-dark-2);margin:0;">The offer was clear to people who already knew the consultant, not to those arriving cold. Weak CTAs, misaligned operational flow, information hierarchy that needed rethinking.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="scope" style="border-color:rgba(232,154,154,0.2);background:rgba(232,154,154,0.04);">
            <h4 style="color:#e89a9a;font-size:15px;font-weight:700;margin-bottom:10px;">02 · Budget at risk on the wrong problem</h4>
            <p style="font-size:14.5px;line-height:23px;color:var(--on-dark-2);margin:0;">A full redesign was on the table. Significant investment to fix a visual problem that was not the actual cause of the low conversion rate.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- Design decision -->
      <div class="holo glow-wine reveal d2" style="margin-top:32px;padding:32px 36px;">
        <div class="eyebrow" style="margin-bottom:12px;">Design decision</div>
        <p style="font-size:19px;font-weight:700;color:#fff;line-height:1.4;margin:0 0 16px;font-family:var(--font-heading);">Deliver less than the client expected.</p>
        <p style="font-size:15px;line-height:24px;color:var(--on-dark-2);margin:0;">UX audit and gap analysis made it clear the problem was structural. The roadmap separated three levels: what to do now (CTAs and operational flow), what not to do (full redesign), what to defer (visual restyling). In parallel, a new dedicated landing page aligned with an advertising specialist.</p>
      </div>

      <!-- Three decisions -->
      <div class="decisions reveal d3" style="margin-top:48px;">
        <div class="eyebrow" style="margin-bottom:24px;">The three decisions</div>
        <div class="decision-item">
          <div class="decision-n">01</div>
          <div>
            <div class="decision-title">Do: realign CTAs and operational flow</div>
            <p style="font-size:14.5px;line-height:23px;color:var(--on-dark-2);margin:6px 0 0;">Targeted interventions on the main friction points. Priority change checklist, alignment with an ADV specialist, new landing page with an optimised flow.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="decision-item">
          <div class="decision-n">02</div>
          <div>
            <div class="decision-title">Don't do: full redesign</div>
            <p style="font-size:14.5px;line-height:23px;color:var(--on-dark-2);margin:6px 0 0;">Approximately €3,000 in budget saved. The problem wasn't aesthetic, and a redesign would have consumed resources without fixing the actual cause of the low conversion rate.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="decision-item">
          <div class="decision-n">03</div>
          <div>
            <div class="decision-title">Defer: visual restyling</div>
            <p style="font-size:14.5px;line-height:23px;color:var(--on-dark-2);margin:6px 0 0;">To be evaluated after measuring the impact of the structural interventions. Conversion data is incoming: ad campaigns need time to produce a reliable signal.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- CTA -->
  <section class="section">
    <div class="shell">
      <div class="cta-band reveal">
        <div class="eyebrow center" style="justify-content:center;">The next case</div>
        <h2 style="margin-top:14px;">Could be yours.</h2>
        <p>Tell me the context in three lines. If it's a good fit, we start with a triage.</p>
        <div class="cta-row"><a class="btn btn-primary btn-lg magnetic" href="https://calendly.com/mirandauxdesigner/30min" target="_blank" rel="noopener"><i data-lucide="calendar-check" class="ic"></i> Book a triage call</a></div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

